## 🧠 Architecture

FleetDash uses an **event-driven architecture** where telemetry is processed asynchronously instead of forcing every operation through the main application thread.

| Layer       | Technology            | Responsibility               |
| ----------- | --------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Frontend    | React 19 + TypeScript | Monitoring dashboard         |
| Runtime     | Node.js               | Backend execution            |
| API         | Express 5             | Telemetry & REST APIs        |
| Database    | MongoDB + Mongoose    | Vehicle & telemetry storage  |
| Messaging   | Redis Pub/Sub         | Event distribution           |
| Concurrency | Worker Threads        | CPU-intensive processing     |
| Geospatial  | Turf.js               | Geofence calculations        |
| Realtime    | Socket.IO             | Live telemetry               |
| Rendering   | Canvas API            | High-frequency visualization |

---

## 📡 Telemetry Model

A vehicle can continuously send data such as:

```json
{
  "vehicleId": "VH-1024",
  "lat": 22.3072,
  "lng": 73.1812,
  "speed": 64,
  "heading": 145,
  "batteryLevel": 82,
  "fuelLevel": 61
}
```

Telemetry is grouped into time-based buckets to reduce unnecessary database overhead.

### MongoDB Bucket Pattern

```text
Vehicle
   │
   ├── Hour 01
   │    ├── Reading
   │    ├── Reading
   │    └── Reading
   │
   ├── Hour 02
   │    ├── Reading
   │    ├── Reading
   │    └── Reading
   │
   └── Hour 03
        ├── Reading
        └── Reading
```

---

## 🌍 Geospatial Intelligence

FleetDash uses **Turf.js** for geospatial operations.

Supported concepts include:

* 📍 Point location tracking
* 🔵 Circular geofences
* 🔷 Polygon geofences
* 🚨 Boundary breach detection
* 📏 Distance calculations
* 🗺️ Spatial containment checks

Example:

```text
             GEOFENCE
        ╭────────────────╮
        │                │
        │      🚗        │
        │                │
        │                │
        ╰────────────────╯
                 │
                 │ vehicle exits
                 ▼
              🚨 ALERT
```

